##### MF1: GENERAL INFORMATION                                    7325 1451
                                                                  7325 1451
- MT451    : Descriptive data and directory                       7325 1451
                                                                  7325 1451
This text and the full directory of used MF/MT sections.          7325 1451
                                                                  7325 1451
##### MF2: RESONANCE PARAMETERS                                   7325 1451
                                                                  7325 1451
- MT151    : Resonance parameters                                 7325 1451
                                                                  7325 1451
Since no resonances data is available for the nucleus, we include 7325 1451
the scattering length only, assuming that the TALYS generated     7325 1451
elastic scattering cross-section at 10^-5 eV incident energy      7325 1451
is due purely to s-wave scattering.                               7325 1451
                                                                  7325 1451
##### MF3: REACTION CROSS SECTIONS                                7325 1451
                                                                  7325 1451
All the data present in the following MT-sections have been       7325 1451
calculated with Talys. If the maximal cross section in an         7325 1451
excitation function over the whole energy range does not exceed   7325 1451
1.e-9 b, the MT-number is not included at all. Cross sections     7325 1451
lower than 1.e-20 b are assumed to have no physical meaning and   7325 1451
are set to zero. Not all of the following MT-numbers may be       7325 1451
present for this isotope, because this depends on Q-values.       7325 1451
They are all listed for completeness.                             7325 1451
                                                                  7325 1451
- MT1      : Total cross section                                  7325 1451
                                                                  7325 1451
Calculated with the optical model over the whole energy range.    7325 1451
                                                                  7325 1451
- MT2      : Elastic scattering cross section                     7325 1451
                                                                  7325 1451
Obtained by subtracting the non-elastic cross section from the    7325 1451
total cross section.                                              7325 1451
                                                                  7325 1451
- MT3      : Non-elastic cross section                            7325 1451
                                                                  7325 1451
Calculated with the optical model over the whole energy range.    7325 1451
                                                                  7325 1451
- MT4      : Total inelastic cross section                        7325 1451
                                                                  7325 1451
Sum of MT=51-91.                                                  7325 1451
                                                                  7325 1451
- MT5      : (n,anything) cross section                           7325 1451
                                                                  7325 1451
For energies below 20 MeV, MT5 contains the lumped (n,gamma x)    7325 1451
cross section, where x may represent neutron, proton, deuteron,   7325 1451
triton, Helium-3 or alpha. Using the relative yields of MF6/MT5,  7325 1451
the (n,gamma n), (n,gamma p), ..., (n,gamma alpha) can be         7325 1451
recovered. These cross sections are relatively small. However,    7325 1451
addition of these cross sections, which can not be stored in any  7325 1451
other MT-number, ensures that the partial cross sections add up   7325 1451
to the non-elastic cross section. Above 20 MeV, MT5 contains the  7325 1451
total non-elastic cross section, with which the information of    7325 1451
MF6/MT5 can be combined to obtain particle production cross       7325 1451
sections and (double-)differential cross sections.                7325 1451
                                                                  7325 1451
- MT11     : (n,2nd) cross section                                7325 1451
- MT16     : (n,2n) cross section                                 7325 1451
- MT17     : (n,3n) cross section                                 7325 1451
- MT22     : (n,na) cross section                                 7325 1451
- MT23     : (n,n3a) cross section                                7325 1451
